[38;5;231m⏺[39m I changed [38;5;153muserId[39m to [38;5;153muser_id[39m in the [38;5;153mGET /users[39m response ([38;5;153mroutes/users.js:6[39m). Nothing else in the repo referenced the
  old name. I haven't committed it, and I didn't run anything to test it.

  [1mDon't ship this as-is.[0m The README says [38;5;153mGET /users[39m field names are part of the API contract, and that changes go
  through a versioned endpoint. It lists three consumers that read this response: the web app, the iOS app (3.2 and
  later), and the nightly partner export. Renaming the field in place would break all three as soon as it's deployed.
  Installed iOS apps can't be fixed until users update.

  Two safer options:
  - [1mVersioned endpoint[0m (what the README calls for): add a new version of the endpoint that returns [38;5;153muser_id[39m, and leave
    the current [38;5;153m/users[39m unchanged.
  - [1mTransition period:[0m return both [38;5;153muserId[39m and [38;5;153muser_id[39m until the consumers have switched, then remove [38;5;153muserId[39m.

  If you already know these consumers are ready for the rename, the change is done and ready to commit. Otherwise, tell
  me which option you want and I'll switch to it.

